      "output": "**Lisbon, Portugal \u2013 a relaxed long\u2011weekend with caf\u00e9 culture and easy mid\u2011morning arrivals**  \n\nLisbon offers a compact historic centre, hills dotted with caf\u00e9s, and a mild climate in spring/autumn, fitting a slow\u2011travel vibe without the need for an early\u2011morning flight from Manchester.\n\n**Day\u202f1 \u2013 Arrival & settle**  \nFly Manchester \u2192 Lisbon (mid\u2011morning, e.g., 10\u202fam). Take the Aerobus to Pra\u00e7a do Com\u00e9rcio, check into a boutique hotel or well\u2011rated Airbnb in Baixa. Lunch at *Caf\u00e9 A Brasileira* (historic caf\u00e9). Afternoon stroll through Alfama, ending with sunset at Miradouro de Santa\u202fLuzia.  \n\n**Day\u202f2 \u2013 Caf\u00e9 hopping & culture**  \nLate\u2011morning brunch at *Nicolau Lisboa* (healthy caf\u00e9). Walk the historic tram 28 route, stopping at S\u00e3o\u202fVicente de Fora church. Lunch at *Time Out Market* (varied stalls). Afternoon: visit the National Tile Museum (Museu Nacional do Azulejo). Evening: dinner at a riverside restaurant in Cais do Sodr\u00e9 and a relaxed drink at *Pens\u00e3o Amor*.\n\n**Day\u202f3 \u2013 Day\u2011long leisure**  \nSleep\u2011in, then coffee at *F\u00e1brica Coffee Roasters*. Explore Bel\u00e9m: Jer\u00f3nimos Monastery, Bel\u00e9m Tower, and try the iconic past\u00e9is de nata at *Past\u00e9is de Bel\u00e9m*. Return to the city centre for a leisurely dinner in the Chiado neighbourhood.  \n\n**Day\u202f4 \u2013 Light morning & departure**  \nBrunch at *The Mill* (Portuguese\u2011Australian caf\u00e9). Stroll through the LX Factory creative hub, browse boutiques and street art. Catch an afternoon flight (e.g., 3\u202fpm) back to Manchester.\n\n**Book now**  \n- Flights (mid\u2011morning outbound, early\u2011afternoon return) \u2013 prices fluctuate, especially around holidays.  \n- Accommodation in Baixa/Chiado (high demand for weekend stays).  \n\n**Decide later**  \n- Specific restaurant reservations (e.g., dinner on Day\u202f2) \u2013 optional, can be booked a few days ahead.  \n- Museum tickets (most are walk\u2011in, but timed entry for the Tile Museum may be advisable in peak season).  \n\n**External checks**  \n- Verify visa\u2011free entry for UK citizens (Portugal is Schengen; post\u2011Brexit rules apply).  \n- Confirm COVID\u201119 entry requirements (if any).  \n- Check weather forecast for your chosen dates to pack appropriately.  \n\nEnjoy a mellow weekend sipping coffee, wandering cobbled streets, and soaking up Lisbon\u2019s laid\u2011back charm.  \n\n*Is the mid\u2011morning outbound flight timing workable for you, or would you prefer a slightly later departure?*",
