      "output": "**Assumption:**\u202fYou follow a 4\u2011day upper/lower split, have dumbbells\u202f(\u224812\u201320\u202fkg) and a pull\u2011up bar at home, and will be equipment\u2011free Thursday\u202f&\u202fFriday while traveling.\n\n**This week (7\u202fdays)**  \n\n| Day | Session | Main moves (sets\u202f\u00d7\u202freps) | Notes |\n|-----|---------|--------------------------|-------|\n| Mon | Upper\u202fA |\u202fDumbbell bench press\u202f3\u00d78\u201110\u202f\u00b7\u202fOne\u2011arm row\u202f3\u00d78\u201110\u202f\u00b7\u202fPull\u2011ups\u202f3\u00d7max\u202f\u00b7\u202fLateral raise\u202f2\u00d712\u201115\u202f\u00b7\u202fTriceps extension\u202f2\u00d712\u201115 | Keep rest 90\u202fs; aim for a weight that\u2019s 2\u20113\u202fRPE below failure. |\n| Tue | Lower\u202fA |\u202fGoblet squat\u202f3\u00d710\u201112\u202f\u00b7\u202fRomanian\u2011dumbbell deadlift\u202f3\u00d78\u201110\u202f\u00b7\u202fBulgarian split squat\u202f2\u00d78\u201110\u202f\u00b7\u202fCalf raise (hold dumbbell)\u202f2\u00d715\u201120\u202f\u00b7\u202fPlank\u202f3\u00d730\u202fs | Rest 90\u202fs; focus on depth and hip hinge. |\n| Wed | Upper\u202fB |\u202fIncline dumbbell press\u202f3\u00d78\u201110\u202f\u00b7\u202fChest\u2011supported reverse fly\u202f2\u00d712\u201115\u202f\u00b7\u202fChin\u2011up\u202f3\u00d7max\u202f\u00b7\u202fArnold press\u202f2\u00d710\u201112\u202f\u00b7\u202fBiceps curl\u202f2\u00d712\u201115 | Same tempo as Mon. |\n| Thu | Travel (no gear) |\u202fBody\u2011weight circuit\u202f3\u202frounds: 20\u202fair\u2011squats\u202f\u00b7\u202f15\u202fpush\u2011ups\u202f\u00b7\u202f30\u202fs\u202fmountain\u2011climbers\u202f\u00b7\u202f10\u202freverse\u2011lunges\u202f\u00b7\u202f30\u202fs\u202fplank | Keep intensity moderate; use a hotel stair if available for extra step\u2011ups. |\n| Fri | Travel (no gear) |\u202fMobility & core\u202f2\u202frounds: 30\u202fs\u202fhip\u2011flexor stretch\u202f\u00b7\u202f30\u202fs\u202fcat\u2011cow\u202f\u00b7\u202f20\u202fbird\u2011dogs\u202f\u00b7\u202f15\u202fsupermans\u202f\u00b7\u202f30\u202fs\u202fside\u2011plank each side | Light, recovery\u2011focused. |\n| Sat | Lower\u202fB |\u202fDumbbell sumo squat\u202f3\u00d710\u201112\u202f\u00b7\u202fSingle\u2011leg deadlift\u202f2\u00d78\u201110\u202f\u00b7\u202fGlute bridge (hold dumbbell)\u202f3\u00d712\u201115\u202f\u00b7\u202fStanding calf raise\u202f2\u00d715\u201120\u202f\u00b7\u202fRussian twist\u202f3\u00d720 | Rest 90\u202fs; maintain good form. |\n| Sun | Rest or active recovery |\u202fLight walk, yoga, foam\u2011roll | \u2013 |\n\n**Progression rule:**\u202fEach week aim to add\u202f\u22482.5\u202fkg to a dumbbell lift or increase a rep\u2011range by\u202f1\u20112\u202freps while keeping the same set scheme. If you miss a session, shift the next workout forward but keep the upper/lower order (e.g., do Upper\u202fB on Saturday and Lower\u202fB on Sunday).\n\n**Busy\u2011week fallback:**\u202fIf you can only fit two days, do Upper\u202fA on Monday and Lower\u202fA on Tuesday; replace the other days with the travel body\u2011weight circuit.\n\n---\n\nDo you have any current injuries or limitations I should know about before finalising the plan?",
