      "output": "**Recommendation:**\u202fPursue a data\u2011science\u2011focused role at a Berlin\u2011based company that will let you transition internally or via a lateral hire, while simultaneously building a portfolio of ML projects and a solid credential (e.g., a specialized bootcamp or part\u2011time master\u2019s).  \n\n**Trade\u2011off:**\u202fYou\u2019ll delay a salary bump for the next 6\u201112\u202fmonths while you acquire the technical depth needed for a data\u2011science title, but the effort makes the move far more sustainable and reduces the risk of being \u201cover\u2011qualified\u201d for junior analyst roles that won\u2019t progress.  \n\n**Next actions**\n\n1. **Skill gap audit & project plan (Week\u202f1).** List the top data\u2011science competencies you lack (e.g., supervised learning, model deployment, cloud ML services). Choose two\u2011to\u2011three real\u2011world projects that use Berlin\u2011relevant datasets (e.g., public transport, e\u2011commerce) and commit to delivering a complete end\u2011to\u2011end pipeline within the next 8\u202fweeks.  \n\n2. **Targeted learning (Weeks\u202f2\u20118).** Enroll in a part\u2011time, reputable program that offers a certificate in data science (e.g., a 3\u2011month bootcamp or a university\u2011affiliated \u201cData Science for Professionals\u201d course). Allocate 8\u201110\u202fhours weekly to cover Python\u2011scikit\u2011learn, SQL\u2011advanced, and cloud (AWS/GCP) deployment.  \n\n3. **Internal/market positioning (Weeks\u202f4\u201112).**  \n   - **Internal:** Schedule a 30\u2011minute career\u2011development chat with your manager to share the project roadmap and ask for a \u201cdata\u2011science stretch\u201d assignment or mentorship.  \n   - **External:** Update your LinkedIn and CV to highlight the new projects, the upcoming certificate, and quantifiable analyst achievements. Begin applying to Berlin data\u2011science roles that list \u201cjunior\u202f/\u202fassociate\u201d as the seniority level (you\u2019ll now meet the technical bar).  \n\nThese steps give you a concrete portfolio, a recognized credential, and a clear signal to employers that you\u2019re ready to move from analyst to data scientist without needing to relocate. Let me know which learning program you\u2019re leaning toward, and I can help you map the weekly study milestones.",
