      "output": "A relaxed long\u2011weekend in **Lisbon, Portugal** fits your love of slow travel, caf\u00e9 culture and avoiding early flights \u2013 you can fly out mid\u2011morning on the first day and return late afternoon on the fourth.\n\n**Draft itinerary**\n\n- **Day\u202f1 \u2013 Arrival & Alfama stroll** \u2013 Mid\u2011morning flight from Manchester to Lisbon, settle in a centrally\u2011located boutique hotel (preferably with a small terrace). Spend the afternoon wandering the historic Alfama district, stopping at a few local caf\u00e9s for pastel de nata and espresso.  \n- **Day\u202f2 \u2013 Bel\u00e9m & riverside caf\u00e9s** \u2013 Take tram 15 to Bel\u00e9m; visit Jer\u00f3nimos Monastery and the Past\u00e9is de Bel\u00e9m bakery. In the afternoon, relax at a riverside caf\u00e9 in the LX\u202fFactory complex, soaking up the creative vibe.  \n- **Day\u202f3 \u2013 Bairro Alto & sunset view** \u2013 Morning at a leisurely pace: brunch at a caf\u00e9 in Pr\u00edncipe Real, then explore the boutique shops. Evening: head to the S\u00e3o\u202fPedro de Alc\u00e2ntara viewpoint for sunset, followed by dinner at a modest tavern with fado music.  \n- **Day\u202f4 \u2013 Market & departure** \u2013 Late\u2011morning visit to Mercado da Ribeira (Time Out Market) for a final food\u2011ie experience, then a relaxed transfer to the airport for an afternoon flight back to Manchester.\n\n**Key points to book now**\n\n- **Flights** \u2013 Mid\u2011morning outbound and late\u2011afternoon return (to avoid early departures).  \n- **Boutique hotel** \u2013 Secure a room with a terrace or garden view; book at least 4\u20136\u202fweeks ahead for best rates.  \n\n**Decide later**\n\n- Specific caf\u00e9 or restaurant reservations (most are walk\u2011in friendly).  \n- Optional day\u2011trip to Sintra if you find extra time; can be arranged on Day\u202f3 afternoon.  \n\n*Quick check:* Verify that your passport is valid for at least six months beyond travel dates and that any COVID\u2011related entry requirements for Portugal are met. Let me know your preferred travel dates or any budget ceiling, and I can refine the plan further.",
