      },
      "output": "Based on what I know (you\u2019re already in the Apple ecosystem and want to keep a phone for\u202f4+\u202fyears while staying under\u202f\u00a3700), the key criteria are:\n\n1. **Long\u2011term software support** \u2013 you\u2019ll want iOS updates for at least five years.  \n2. **Battery life & durability** \u2013 a phone that can comfortably last a full day with moderate use and survive daily wear.  \n3. **Camera quality that\u2019s good enough for casual shooting** \u2013 sharp enough for social media but not a professional\u2011grade system.  \n4. **Price\u2011to\u2011value balance** \u2013 fits comfortably under your \u00a3700 ceiling.\n\n### Recommendation  \n**iPhone SE (3rd\u202fgen, 2022)** \u2013 typically \u00a3429\u2013\u00a3479 (new).  \n- Same A15 Bionic chip as the iPhone\u202f13, guaranteeing iOS updates for many years.  \n- Compact 4.7\u2011inch display, solid glass front/back with IP67 water resistance.  \n- Single\u2011camera system that still produces very good photos and 4K video.  \n- Battery life is decent for its size; a spare power\u2011bank can cover the occasional long day.  \n\n### Runner\u2011up  \n**iPhone\u202f13 (standard, 128\u202fGB)** \u2013 typically \u00a3599\u2013\u00a3649 (refurbished or on sale).  \n- Larger 6.1\u2011inch OLED display and dual\u2011camera system for better low\u2011light shots.  \n- Slightly longer battery life than the SE.  \n- Still receives iOS updates for the same period, but the higher price pushes you closer to your budget limit.\n\n**Decisive trade\u2011off:** The SE gives you the longest software runway for the lowest cost, while the iPhone\u202f13 offers a bigger screen and better camera at a modest premium. If you value a larger display and extra camera flexibility, the iPhone\u202f13 is worth the extra spend; otherwise the SE is the more economical, future\u2011proof choice.\n\n**Next step:** Check current listings for both models (new, certified\u2011refurbished, or reputable used) to confirm they fall within your price range and decide whether the larger screen of the iPhone\u202f13 is worth the extra \u00a3150\u2011\u00a3200 for you.",
