      },
      "output": "**Assumption:** You need a cash deposit for a flat in Dublin\u202f\u2248\u202f3\u202fyears (36\u202fmonths). The target amount will depend on the price you expect and the typical 10\u201115\u202f% deposit required.\n\n### How to set the target\n1. **Estimate the flat price** \u2013 Look up recent listings in the neighbourhoods you\u2019re interested in and note a realistic upper\u2011range price (e.g., \u20ac300k\u2011\u20ac350k).  \n2. **Apply the deposit rule\u2011of\u2011thumb** \u2013 In Ireland, most lenders expect 10\u201115\u202f% of the purchase price as cash down\u2011payment.  \n   *\u202f10\u202f% of \u20ac300k\u202f=\u202f\u20ac30k  \n   *\u202f15\u202f% of \u20ac350k\u202f=\u202f\u20ac52.5k  \n   Choose a figure that feels comfortable; a common middle ground is **\u20ac40k**.  \n\n3. **Add a safety buffer** \u2013 Because property prices can rise and unexpected costs (legal fees, moving expenses) appear, add ~5\u202f% of the target as a buffer.  \n   *\u202f5\u202f% of \u20ac40k\u202f\u2248\u202f\u20ac2k  \n\n**Savings target:** **\u2248\u202f\u20ac42,000** over 36\u202fmonths.\n\n### What this means for cash flow\n- Required monthly saving\u202f\u2248\u202f\u20ac42,000\u202f\u00f7\u202f36\u202f\u2248\u202f**\u20ac1,170**.  \n- If you already have some cash saved, subtract that amount from the total and spread the remainder over the remaining months.\n\n### Down\u2011side test\nIf a bad month reduces your net income by \u20ac500, you could:\n- **Temporarily cut the monthly contribution** to \u20ac670 (still on track, just slower).  \n- **Extend the horizon** by a few months (e.g., add 6\u202fmonths, turning the plan into 42\u202fmonths, which lowers the monthly need to \u2248\u202f\u20ac1,000).  \n- **Use the buffer** (the extra \u20ac2k) to cover a few shortfalls without breaking the schedule.\n\n### Quick next actions\n1. **Research current flat listings** in your target area and note a realistic price range.  \n2. **Calculate your existing cash** earmarked for the deposit; subtract it from \u20ac42k to get the remaining amount.  \n3. **Create a simple spreadsheet** with a column for each month, entering the required \u20ac1,170 (or adjusted figure) and a column for any shortfall or surplus to monitor progress.  \n\nIf the monthly amount feels unaffordable, consider a licensed financial adviser to explore budgeting tweaks or low\u2011risk savings vehicles.",
